-- title:
--   Lemma 3.3 — $C_0$ preserves every $R_i$ and the monomial flag: $C_0^j(m_a)=(-1)^{j\sum a_i}m_a+\sum_{b<a}c_bm_b$, $c_b\in R_0$
-- statement:
--   In the height-$h$ second Garcia–Stichtenoth tower over $k=\mathbb F_{q^2}$ ($q=p^s>2$, $h\ge1$), let $R_0=k[x_0,t^{-1}]$ and $R_i=R_{i-1}[x_i]$. The operator $C_0$ preserves every $R_i$, $0\le i\le h$. Order the standard monomials lexicographically with the highest tower coordinate compared first. For every integer $j\ge0$ and every $a$,
--   $$C_0^j(m_a)=(-1)^{j\sum_i a_i}\,m_a+\sum_{b<a}c_b(x_0)\,m_b,\qquad c_b\in R_0.\qquad(3.13)$$
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the tower F_h of (3.1) over k = F_{q^2}, q = p^s > 2 → any field F over any finite field k with q^2 elements (IsPrimePow q, 2 < q), with x_0 transcendental, (x_i^q + x_i)(1 + x_{i-1}^{q-1}) = x_{i-1}^q for 1 ≤ i ≤ h, and F = k(x_0, …, x_h) (IsGSTower); reason: every such F is a model of F_h; the division in φ is cleared, which excludes no instance
--   - encoding: places P and ord_P normalized to value group Z → Place k F: additive valuations F → Z ∪ {∞}, onto Z, zero on k^×; reason: places of a function field correspond one to one to their normalized valuations
--   - encoding: R_i = R_{i−1}[x_i], R_0 = k[x_0, t^{−1}]; coefficients c_b(x_0) ∈ R_0 → R_i the k-subalgebra of F generated by x_0, t^{−1}, x_1, …, x_i; c_b elements of F lying in R_0; reason: the same rings, as subrings of F
-- source:
--   Chao, Liu, Li, Ma, Wang, Quasilinear Encoding at the Quadratic Alphabet Scale via Short Cartier Bases, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 355c15dc…), p. 10, Lemma 3.3, (3.13) (PDF p. 12)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QuasilinearAG_Encoding_Tower

namespace QuasilinearAG.Encoding

open Classical in
/-- Lemma 3.3 (Preservation of the monomial flag), p. 10 (PDF 12). In the height-`h` second
Garcia–Stichtenoth tower over `k = F_{q²}` (`q > 2` a prime power), the zeroth Cartier coefficient
`C₀` maps every localized ring `R_i = k[x₀, t⁻¹, x₁, …, x_i]` (`0 ≤ i ≤ h`) into itself, and for
every `j ≥ 0` and every standard monomial `m_a`,
`C₀^j(m_a) = (-1)^{j Σ_i a_i} m_a + Σ_{b < a} c_b m_b` with every `c_b ∈ R₀`, where `b < a` is
the lexicographic order comparing the highest tower coordinate first (3.13). -/
theorem lemma_3_3 {k F : Type*} [Field k] [Fintype k] [Field F] [Algebra k F]
    (q h : ℕ) (hq : IsPrimePow q) (hq2 : 2 < q) (hk : Fintype.card k = q ^ 2) (hh : 1 ≤ h)
    (x : ℕ → F) (hx : IsGSTower k q h x) :
    (∀ i ≤ h, ∀ f ∈ towerRing (k := k) q x i, cartierCoeff q (towerT q x) 0 f ∈ towerRing (k := k) q x i) ∧
      ∀ (j : ℕ) (a : Fin h → Fin q), ∃ c : (Fin h → Fin q) → F,
        (∀ b, c b ∈ towerRing (k := k) q x 0) ∧
        (cartierCoeff q (towerT q x) 0)^[j] (stdMono q h x a) =
          (-1 : F) ^ (j * ∑ i, (a i : ℕ)) * stdMono q h x a +
            ∑ b ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun b => colexLT b a), c b * stdMono q h x b := by sorry

end QuasilinearAG.Encoding
